<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Heiton half-yr pre-tax profit up 22 pct.</title>
<headline>Heiton half-yr pre-tax profit up 22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to October 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.47		   vs 5.36</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.65		   vs 0.95</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    4.65		   vs 3.81</p>
<p> Turnover		   71.80		  vs 66.41</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.24		   vs 0.40</p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.68		   vs 1.37</p>
<p> Net taxed		  2.98		   vs 2.44</p>
<p> Profit retained	  2.21		   vs 2.00</p>
<p> Registration date	Jan 28</p>
<p> Pay date		   April 7</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 Jan 20</p>
<p>NOTE - Building materials group Heiton Holdings Plc said operating margins improved to 6.8 percent from 6.3 percent in the first half of 1995 while net operating cashflow totalled 3.5 million punts.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 661 3377</p>
</text>
